cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use PhyloSlicer, please cite it as below, and cite the treesliceR method paper that introduced the temporal-slicing paradigm."
title: "PhyloSlicer: temporal slicing of phylogenies and cumulative-diversity rate analysis for macroecology in Python"
abstract: >-
  Independent, vectorised Python implementation of slicing phylogenies to infer
  phylogenetic patterns over evolutionary time. Expresses slicing as a single
  (E, k) interval-intersection contribution matrix so no tree is copied per
  slice, and adds sparse-matrix diversity indices (PD, PE, PB and its
  turnover-weighted variant), certified cumulative-diversity rate fitting with
  convergence diagnostics, posterior-tree uncertainty quantification, spatial
  adjacency helpers, and a command-line interface. Cross-validated against
  treesliceR v1.1.0.
